## Anti Patterns

### 1. Storing Private Data in Events

```typescript
// Không nên - sensitive data in events
interface UserCreatedEvent {
    payload: {
        userId: string;
        email: string;
        passwordHash: 'sha256:abc123...', // Don't store!
        ssn: '123-45-6789', // Don't store!
    }
}

// Nên - only store necessary data
interface UserCreatedEvent {
    payload: {
        userId: string;
        email: string;
        // No sensitive data
    }
}
```

### 2. Events that Mutate Other Aggregates

```typescript
// Không nên - cross-aggregate mutation
interface OrderConfirmedEvent {
    payload: {
        orderId: string;
        // Don't include inventory changes here!
        inventoryUpdated: true,
        stockLevel: 100
    }
}

// Nên - single aggregate responsibility
interface OrderConfirmedEvent {
    payload: {
        orderId: string;
        paymentId: string;
    }
}
// Inventory update is a separate aggregate's responsibility
```

### 3. Command vs Event Confusion

```typescript
// Không nên - naming as command
const event = { eventType: 'CreateUserCommand' }; // Wrong!

// Nên - use past tense for events
const event = { eventType: 'UserCreated' }; // Correct
```

### 4. Large Event Payloads

```typescript
// Không nên - huge payload
interface SystemSnapshotEvent {
    payload: {
        allUsers: User[], // All users in system!
        allOrders: Order[], // All orders!
        allProducts: Product[] // All products!
    }
}

// Nên - granular, atomic events
interface UserCreatedEvent { payload: { user: User } }
interface OrderCreatedEvent { payload: { order: Order } }
```

### 5. No Versioning Strategy

```typescript
// Không nên - no schema version
interface Event {
    payload: { name: string }
}

// Nên - include version
interface Event {
    metadata: { schemaVersion: '2.0' }
    payload: { firstName: string; lastName: string } // v2
}
```

